      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "3",
          "section": "II.C Heat Treatments",
          "quote": "Finally, a super-solidus hot isostatic pressing heat treatment was performed, consisting of a heating ramp of 20 °C/min and two isothermal stages, both at super-solidus temperatures. The two isothermal stages consist of 4 hours at 1365 °C and 6 hours at 1370 °C, after which the specimens were quenched to obtain a fine and homogeneous distribution of the γ/γ’ microstructure.",
          "table": null,
